# Concerted Care gives hexproof until end of turn: after it resolves on Bot1's Llanowar Elves, Bot2's Lightning Bolt cannot be
# cast at the Elves (the refusal), but it can be cast at Bot1's Ornithopter (the positive control: same Bolt, a creature
# without hexproof), which dies. The Elves were not the only target in play, so the refusal is for hexproof.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Bofur, Reliable Guardian
Forest
Forest x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Bofur, Reliable Guardian.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves; Ability: Adventure)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = Hexproof; Indestructible
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Exile = Bofur, Reliable Guardian
